Subject: Getting differential methylation of a subset of merged samples
Message-ID: <FkITJM7skd0.Qi98VOEZBgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/FkITJM7skd0/m/Qi98VOEZBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I have four groups of related samples, I'll call them groups A,B,C,D. I want to make 4 pairwise comparisons (A vs. B, B vs. C etc.) to get differential methylation information. However, I want only the CpGs present that are represented in all 4 groups, so that I can look up the methylation value of any CpG that is significant in the A vs. B comparison in the C vs. D comparsion for example. Is there any way to merge all 4 groups but only compare 2 at a time?

From uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com  Tue May  8 19:49:32 2018
From: uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com (Altuna Akalin)
Date: Tue, 08 May 2018 19:49:32 +0000
