Message-ID: <FkITJM7skd0.abU0cYf4AQAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <FkITJM7skd0.Qi98VOEZBgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
References: <FkITJM7skd0.Qi98VOEZBgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/FkITJM7skd0/m/abU0cYf4AQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You can make a methylBase object with A,B,C,D and use reorganize() to make methylBase objects with A-B, B-C etc. and run calculateDiffMeth separately on each new methylBase object.

Best,
Altuna

