Hi,

I wish to find out methylation status of DMPK gene in BS converted amplicon samples. For this purpose, I processed the raw reads with trim_galore and followed the bismark pipeline for genome_preparation, bismark alignement, deduplication and bismark_methylation_extraction. I used human genomic DMPK gene sequence (link_to_reference <https://useast.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Sequence?g=ENSG00000104936;r=19:45769717-45782552>) as a reference and mapped the samples against this FASTA file. After this I used deduplicate bismark to obtain a deduplicated bam file. This bam file was sorted and indexed using samtools.

I used processBismarkAln command and got a myobj from bam file.

myobj=processBismarkAln( location =
                                "C:/Users/kalyani_patankar/Desktop/S5/pe.deduplicated_sorted.bam",
                              sample.id="S5", assembly="hg38",
                              read.context="CpG", save.folder="C:/Users/kalyani_patankar/Desktop/S5/methCall")

After This I followed the commands:

library(genomation)

gene.obj = readTranscriptFeatures(location = "C:/Users/kalyani_patankar/Desktop/S5/DMPK.bed")

annotate.WithGenicParts(myobj, gene.obj)

DMPK.bed is a bed file obtained from UCSC genome browser

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-8ZLFNcJ6NcU/WwbqG5-tZCI/AAAAAAAAAlw/oZxOgT31g88vmF4B8yFPKQcelNyeqEaaACLcBGAs/s1600/Capture.JPG>

I am getting the following error when I run this command.

Error in annotate.WithGenicParts(myobj, gene.obj) :
  unused arguments (myobj, gene.obj)

How Can I resolve this?

Thanks In Advance

